 To create a React application with the specified features using Visual Studio Code on OSX, follow these steps:

**Step 1:** First, make sure you have Node.js installed. You can download it from https://nodejs.org/. After installation, verify the installation by running `node --version` and `npm --version` in your terminal.

**Step 2:** Open Visual Studio Code and create a new React project by pressing `Ctrl+Shift+P`, typing `React: Create new React app`, and selecting the default settings.

**Step 3:** Navigate to your newly created project directory in the terminal using `cd <your_project_name>`.

**Step 4:** Install Axios for making HTTP requests by running `npm install axios`.

**Step 5:** Create a new component called `TemplateComponent.js` under the `src` folder. In this file, write the following code:

```javascript
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import axios from 'axios';

const TemplateComponent = () => {
  const [template, setTemplate] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchData = async () => {
      try {
        const response = await axios.get('http://localhost:8080/template');
        setTemplate(response.data);
      } catch (error) {
        console.error(error);
      }
    };

    fetchData();
  }, []);

  return (
    <div>
      {template && (
        <>
          <p>{template.sentence}</p>
          {template.choices.relevance.map((option, index) => (
            <select key={index}>
              <option value={option}>{option}</option>
            </select>
          ))}
          {template.choices.quantity.map((option, index) => (
            <select key={index}>
              <option value={option}>{option}</option>
            </select>
          ))}
          <button>Submit</button>
        </>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default TemplateComponent;
```

